# Bump version on every commit

When the user asks to commit (or to commit and push), bump the patch version in the same commit.

- Source of truth: `apps/web/package.json` (`version`). That value is what the UI and service worker show.
- Also bump `apps/api/package.json` and the root `package.json` to the same number.
- If `package-lock.json` records those workspace versions, update them too.
- Do not bump for no-op commits, docs-only work the user asks to skip, or when they explicitly say not to bump.
- Patch bump: `1.0.8` → `1.0.9`. Use minor/major only if they ask.
- Put the version in the commit message (for example `Show written reviews on the profile (1.0.9)`).
